<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijayalaya Chola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 848–871</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijayalaya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> was the founder of the imperial Chola dynasty of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. A local chief claiming descent from the early Cholas, he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> from the Muttaraiyar chiefs around 848 and made it his capital, at first as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Pallavas. His successors built from this base the Chola Empire, which came to dominate southern India and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vijayalaya-chola.jpg" alt="Vijayalaya Chola" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Venu62 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vijayalaya_territories.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
